            <div xml:id="d628">

                <pb facs="0645" n="635" sameAs="frus:frus1937v05/pg635"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.52/2421</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Daniels</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 5693</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-11-18">November 18, 1937</date>.<lb/>[Received November
                        22.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that Mr. Boal
                    had an interview at the Foreign Office on November 15, 1937, with Licenciado
                    Beteta.</p>
                <pb facs="0646" n="636" xml:id="pg636"/>
                <p>The originals of the attached memoranda on various points of interest to the
                    American landowners in the Yaqui Valley, Sonora, were left with Mr. Beteta.</p>
                <p>A copy of this despatch, with enclosures, has been mailed to Vice Consul Yepis in
                    order that he may, in his discretion, verbally advise the American landowners of
                    this action on the part of the Embassy.</p>
                <p>Mr. Boal’s conversation with Mr. Beteta is being reported in a separate
                    despatch.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Josephus Daniels</hi></signed></closer>







